## 7. Core Components

## 7.1 Buttons

### Primary Button

```css
.button-primary {
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  background: var(--text-main);
  color: var(--text-inverse);
  padding: 10px 18px;
  font-family: var(--font-ui);
  font-weight: 600;
  border: none;
  transition:
    transform 160ms ease,
    opacity 160ms ease,
    box-shadow 160ms ease;
}

.button-primary:hover {
  transform: translateY(-1px);
  opacity: 0.92;
}
```

Rules:

* Primary CTAs should be solid by default.
* Do not use gradient buttons as the default CTA style.
* Use gradient only for active AI or progress-related states.

### Secondary Button

```css
.button-secondary {
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  background: var(--surface-card);
  color: var(--text-main);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  padding: 9px 16px;
}
```

### Ghost Button

```css
.button-ghost {
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  border: none;
}
```

---

## 7.2 Input Surfaces

Use input surfaces for prompts, research tasks, comments, follow-ups, and agent controls.

```css
.input-surface {
  background: var(--surface-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
}
```

Rules:

* Inputs should feel calm and trustworthy.
* Use clear placeholder text.
* Keep input icons monochrome by default.
* Keep send actions visually distinct.
* Avoid flashy AI prompt boxes.

---

## 7.3 Mode Selector

Use mode selectors for selecting user intent, task mode, or writing style.

Rules:

* Use compact pills, segmented controls, or subtle step-like selectors.
* Selected state may use `--brand-blue` or a soft pastel tint.
* Inactive states should remain pale and quiet.
* Do not make inactive options look disabled unless they are actually unavailable.
* Do not use completed-state checkmarks unless the component is truly showing completed progress.

Example:

```css
.mode-pill {
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  padding: 8px 14px;
  background: var(--surface-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-ui);
  transition:
    background 160ms ease,
    color 160ms ease,
    transform 160ms ease;
}

.mode-pill.is-selected {
  background: rgba(172, 206, 234, 0.28);
  color: var(--text-main);
}

.mode-pill:hover {
  transform: translateY(-1px);
}
```

---

