## 7.5 Cards and Panels

Use cards and panels for agent outputs, summaries, tools, documents, drafts, and review feedback.

```css
.card {
  background: var(--surface-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-quiet);
}
```

Rules:

* Cards should support content, not become decoration.
* Avoid oversized generic feature cards.
* Avoid giving every card equal weight.
* Use hierarchy inside cards: label, title, summary, metadata, action.
* Keep research cards compact and content-driven.

---

## 7.6 Status Pills

Use status pills for task status, tool status, approval states, and review signals.

Recommended statuses:

* running
* done
* waiting for human
* needs review
* error
* ready
* used as context

Example:

```css
.status-pill {
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  padding: 4px 10px;
  font-size: var(--text-xs);
  font-family: var(--font-ui);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  background: var(--surface-subtle);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.status-pill.done {
  background: var(--success-bg);
  color: var(--success-text);
}

.status-pill.needs-review {
  background: var(--review-bg);
  color: var(--review-text);
}

.status-pill.waiting {
  background: var(--warning-bg);
  color: var(--warning-text);
}
```

---

## 7.7 Source Chips and Citation Chips

Use chips to show sources, citations, uploaded files, tools, or context.

```css
.source-chip {
  border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  padding: 5px 10px;
  background: var(--surface-card-solid);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--text-xs);
}
```

Rules:

* Source chips should be specific when possible.
* Prefer labels like `arXiv · recent papers` over generic labels like `source`.
* Citation chips should feel trustworthy and connected to content.
* Avoid making chips overly colorful.

---

## 7.8 Tool Blocks

Use tool blocks to show agent tools, operations, or background execution.

Rules:

* Tool blocks should be clickable when details exist.
* They should show tool name, status, short summary, and time used when available.
* Selected tool blocks may use a subtle brand-blue outline or background.
* Do not make tool blocks look like decorative feature cards.

Example:

```css
.tool-block {
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-subtle);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  padding: 14px 16px;
  transition:
    border-color 160ms ease,
    background 160ms ease,
    transform 160ms ease;
}

.tool-block:hover {
  transform: translateY(-1px);
  border-color: rgba(172, 206, 234, 0.72);
}

.tool-block.is-selected {
  border-color: var(--brand-blue);
  background: rgba(172, 206, 234, 0.12);
}
```

---

## 7.9 Detail Panels

Use detail panels to show selected item details, tool input/output, citations, sources, review comments, or artifact metadata.

Rules:

* Keep detail panels readable and dense.
* Use clear section labels.
* Use mono font for JSON-like previews.
* Avoid turning details into decorative cards.
* Make selected state clear when detail content changes.

JSON preview style:

```css
.json-preview {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  background: var(--code-bg);
  color: var(--code-text);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: 14px;
  overflow: auto;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
```

---

## 7.10 Code Blocks and LaTeX Blocks

```css
.code-block {
  background: var(--code-bg);
  color: var(--code-text);
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: 20px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  overflow: auto;
}
```

Syntax guidance:

```css
.token.keyword {
  color: var(--brand-blue);
}

.token.string {
  color: var(--brand-yellow);
}

.token.function {
  color: var(--brand-orange);
}

.token.comment {
  color: var(--text-soft);
}
```

Rules:

* Use dark code blocks for contrast.
* Avoid harsh neon syntax colors.
* Keep code readable.
* Use copy buttons with monochrome icons.

---

## 8. Voice, AI Active State, and Aurora Glow

Voice or active AI states may use local glow.

Default state:

* Icons are monochrome.
* No strong glow.
* No large animation.

Active listening / active thinking state:

* Relevant icon may use a pastel gradient.
* The active container may receive a very soft aurora glow.
* Grainy noise may appear only inside the glow layer.
* The animation should feel slow and breathing.

Example:

```css
.ai-active {
  position: relative;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
}

.ai-active::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: -8px;
  z-index: -1;
  border-radius: inherit;
  background: var(--gradient-progress);
  filter: blur(24px);
  opacity: 0.22;
  animation: aurora-breathe 3.6s ease-in-out infinite;
}

.ai-active::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: -8px;
  z-index: -1;
  border-radius: inherit;
  opacity: 0.10;
  pointer-events: none;
  background-image: url("/noise.svg");
  mix-blend-mode: soft-light;
  animation: grain-shift 4s steps(6) infinite;
}
```

Animations:

```css
@keyframes aurora-breathe {
  0%, 100% {
    opacity: 0.16;
    transform: scale(0.985);
  }
  50% {
    opacity: 0.30;
    transform: scale(1.012);
  }
}

@keyframes grain-shift {
  0% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
  25% { transform: translate(-1%, 1%); }
  50% { transform: translate(1%, -1%); }
  75% { transform: translate(-0.5%, -1%); }
  100% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
}
```

Rules:

* Use glow only for active AI, active voice, active progress, or important execution states.
* Do not apply glow to every card.
* Do not use bright neon.
* Do not animate while users are reading long text unless the animation is extremely subtle.

---

## 9. Motion System

```css
:root {
  --motion-fast: 140ms;
  --motion-normal: 220ms;
  --motion-slow: 420ms;
  --motion-breathing: 3600ms;

  --ease-standard: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  --ease-soft: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}
```

Motion rules:

* Use short transitions for hover and selection.
* Use slower motion for AI active states.
* Prefer opacity, transform, and blur.
* Avoid layout-shifting animations.
* Avoid bouncing, spinning, or playful elastic effects.

---

## 10. Icons

Rules:

* Icons should be monochrome by default.
* Use `--text-main`, `--text-muted`, or `--brand-blue`.
* Only active AI, listening, or execution states may use gradient icons.
* Avoid mixed-color icon sets.
* Avoid generic glowing AI icons.

Avoid using these as primary product symbols:

* magic wand
* sparkles
* robot
* rocket
* brain
* abstract AI orb

Prefer symbols related to:

* document
* text
* citation
* tool
* progress
* file
* review
* approval
* search
* export
* microphone
* upload

---

## 11. Accessibility

Rules:

* Maintain sufficient text contrast.
* Do not rely on color alone to indicate state.
* Use labels, icons, or text status alongside color.
* Keep focus states visible.
* Respect reduced motion preferences.

